summary: omelasticsearch TLS sanity — basic HTTPS, TLS version, ciphersuites, PQC key exchange
description: |
    Verify that rsyslog can forward log messages to an Elasticsearch
    instance over TLS using the omelasticsearch module, and validate
    the tls.tlsversion, tls.ciphersuites, and tls.keyexchangegroups
    parameters (upstream PR #7278). Tests include baseline HTTPS
    delivery, TLS 1.3 version enforcement, invalid version rejection,
    ciphersuite selection, and PQC hybrid key exchange with classical
    fallback (X25519MLKEM768:X25519, gated on OpenSSL 3.5+).
contact: Patrik Koncity <pkoncity@redhat.com>
test: ./runtest.sh
require+:
  - library(distribution/dpcommon)
  - library(selinux-policy/common)
  - initscripts
  - rsyslog-elasticsearch
  - openssl
  - patch
  - net-tools
  - java-openjdk
duration: 15m
enabled: true
tag:
  - NoRHEL4
  - NoRHEL5
  - NoRHEL6
  - NoRHEL7
  - NoRHEL8
  - Tier2
adjust:
  - enabled: false
    when: arch == s390x,ppc64le,ia64
    continue: false
/rsa:
    environment:
        CRYPTO_ALG: RSA
    id: daadc7b7-92e7-4fab-9fcf-be01dfc72181
/pqc_alg:
    environment:
        CRYPTO_ALG: ML-DSA-65
    continue: false
    adjust+:
      - enabled: false
        because: PQC it's not implement for ElasticSearch
      - enabled: false
        when: distro < rhel-10.1 or distro < fedora-43
        because: PQC is available from this version of OS
    id: 4a254740-c0ff-4424-ab5c-8ef540c190fd
